# An importer's calls would give a public function compile-time values
# its module never checks: one whose integer parameter sizes an array,
# in its signature, its body, or a function it passes the parameter to,
# is rejected where it is declared, as a generic function is.

use lib

sub main()
  print(lib.plain[2]())

# error: 1:9: public function `zeros` sizes an array by its compile-time parameter `n`; such functions cannot cross module boundaries yet
# error: 8:9: public function `show` sizes an array by its compile-time parameter `k`; such functions cannot cross module boundaries yet
